# Subtest: .skip-all and .push-all on slipping slippy iterators
    1..4
    # Subtest: IterateOneWithoutPhasers
        1..2
        ok 1 - sink-all sinks all the values
        ok 2 - push-all pushes all the values
    ok 1 - IterateOneWithoutPhasers
    # Subtest: IterateOneWithPhasers
        1..2
        ok 1 - sink-all sinks all the values
        ok 2 - push-all pushes all the values
    ok 2 - IterateOneWithPhasers
    # Subtest: IterateTwoWithoutPhasers
        1..2
        ok 1 - sink-all sinks all the values
        ok 2 - push-all pushes all the values
    ok 3 - IterateTwoWithoutPhasers
    # Subtest: IterateMoreWithPhasers
        1..2
        ok 1 - sink-all sinks all the values
        ok 2 - push-all pushes all the values
    ok 4 - IterateMoreWithPhasers
ok 53 - .skip-all and .push-all on slipping slippy iterators
# Subtest: Seq.skip does not leave original Seq consumable
    1..4
    # Subtest: uncached, .skip()
        1..2
        # Subtest: original got consumed
            1..2
            ok 1 - code dies
            ok 2 - right exception type (X::Seq::Consumed)
        ok 1 - original got consumed
        ok 2 - skipped has right content
    ok 1 - uncached, .skip()
    # Subtest: uncached, .skip(n)
        1..2
        # Subtest: original got consumed
            1..2
            ok 1 - code dies
            ok 2 - right exception type (X::Seq::Consumed)
        ok 1 - original got consumed
        ok 2 - skipped has right content
    ok 2 - uncached, .skip(n)
    # Subtest: cached, .skip()
        1..2
        ok 1 - original gives all values
        ok 2 - skipped has right content
    ok 3 - cached, .skip()
    # Subtest: cached, .skip(n)
        1..2
        ok 1 - original gives all values
        ok 2 - skipped has right content
    ok 4 - cached, .skip(n)
ok 54 - Seq.skip does not leave original Seq consumable
# Subtest: Any:U.skip works with Callable
    1..3
    ok 1 - *-1
    ok 2 - *-1
    ok 3 - *-99999
ok 55 - Any:U.skip works with Callable
